/* Sacrament RPG: the gear list. THIS IS THE FILE TO EDIT to change what a hero can carry or cast.
   One entry per line, in the quoted-name style you can see below. The character sheet, the table's server and the Rules page all read this one file.
   id         a short unique word (letters only). Heroes already saved keep their gear by this word, so do not change an id that has been used.
   name       what the player sees.            kind    weapon, armour, supply, relic or grimoire.
   equippable  leave it out and the type decides: everything except a supply can be equipped, and a supply never can (it works from the pack). Put "equippable": false or true to override one item.
   slots      how many of a hero's ten slots it takes (a hero has ten for what is equipped and ten for the pack).
   does       the sentence a player reads.     defence armour's Defence bonus (armour and shield together never add more than +5).
   hearts     extra Hearts while worn.         uses    how many times a supply can be used.
   roll / effort / cat / band   the stat rolled, the Effort die size, which kind of Effort (basic, weapons, guns, magic, ultimate) and how far it reaches.
   horror     how much it raises the Rising Horror each time it is used: a whole number, or dice in quotes, rolled at the moment of use ("d6", "d4+2").
   temptsHorror   true on non-healing spells, grimoires and magic items. Healing spells are false and cost 0; all other spells cost 1.
   Spells sit under "spells"; a grimoire lists its spells by id. A spell with no "cat" has no Effort die; with no "roll" either, it is cast without a check.
   pick       on a grimoire: the number of random spell choices; pickDie is the die rolled (defaults to pick) and the reader casts the spell that comes up, in the order the spells are listed. Its spells cannot be chosen. Relics are finds the GM gives out: a player cannot pick one from the sheet.
   "found" is the d100 loot table: things a hero comes across. A player cannot pick these either; the GM rolls for them (Roll loot) or gives them out. Each has:
   loot       [from, to]: the d100 numbers that give it (every number from 1 to 100 belongs to exactly one item or sub-table; items in the other lists can carry one too).
   table      the sub-table it is on instead of the d100 (its "loot" numbers are then that table's die). Leave it out for the d100.
   Sub-tables are listed under "tables": an id (letters only), a name, the die it rolls ("die": 8 for a d8), and "loot": the numbers that lead into it, on the d100
   (or, with "on": "<another table's id>", on that table; no more than three tables deep). Every number on every table belongs to exactly one thing.
   flavour    the line printed under the name.   category   Mundane, Weapon, Armour, Tool, Consumable, Valuable, Curio, Relic or Grimoire (what it is called, not how it plays).
   cat / roll   WHEN A HERO USES AN ITEM: if it has a "cat" (an Effort kind) the table makes a check with the stat in "roll", and on a success rolls that Effort's die for them,
                plus their bonus in that kind. No "cat" means the item never rolls. A grimoire is used through its spells (each spell has its own cat and roll).
   Notes only the GM may read never go in this file (it is sent to every browser). They are kept on the server, in netlify/functions/_shared/loot-notes.mjs. */
